  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For the exact complex Motakis realization X over S^4, E = X direct-sum X, and operators S,T in B(E) constructed in Horváth--Kania Theorem 5.1 and frozen in source.md and problem.md, the component groups satisfy I(B(E)) is isomorphic to Z/2 and I(M_2(B(E))) is trivial. The nonidentity element is [I_E-2ST]. Therefore ker(s_{B(E)}) = {[I_E],[I_E-2ST]} is isomorphic to Z/2, and [I_E-2ST] has order exactly two.",
